---
const asks = [
  { name: "Speak MCP or run a CLI.", body: "Any agent that can run a shell command can use the CLI; agents that support MCP get the same tools natively." },
  { name: "Work inside the token it's given.", body: "And ask for more through escalation, with evidence." },
  { name: "Submit changes as applications.", body: "With the intent stated and the evidence attached." },
];
const jobs = [
  { name: "Set intent", body: "Decide what to build and why, and what “done” means." },
  { name: "Own contracts", body: "Define and approve the promises components make." },
  { name: "Set risk policy", body: "Decide which areas are sensitive and which rules are hard floors." },
  { name: "Review what matters", body: "High-risk semantic changes, new outside dependencies, and the rules of the game." },
  { name: "Audit", body: "Regularly sample work that was approved without a person." },
  { name: "Own outcomes", body: "When something slips through, fix the system, not just the bug." },
];
---

<section class="section wrap agents" aria-labelledby="agents-title">
  <h2 class="section-title" id="agents-title">Bring your own agent.</h2>
  <div class="agents-grid">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Onus is not an agent, and it doesn't pick one for you. Teams bring the agents they already use,
        whether that's Codex, Claude Code or something they built themselves, and Onus governs all of them the
        same way. It already assumes any agent might be confused or tricked, so it never relies on what happens
        inside one. Every check lives in the doors, the tokens, the environments and the judge.
      </p>
      <p>
        Trust is earned per setup, not per brand. Track records attach to the tool, model, configuration and
        team running it, and a new setup starts in stricter lanes until its results earn it faster ones.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="asks">
      <p class="subhead">Everything Onus asks of an agent</p>
      <ul role="list">
        {
          asks.map((a) => (
            <li>
              <strong>{a.name}</strong> {a.body}
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="muted">No required SDK, no special model, no fine-tuning.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="swap">
    If a team swapped every agent it uses overnight, none of the rules, lanes or review surfaces should need
    to change. Only the track records would start fresh.
  </p>

  <div class="humans">
    <div class="prose">
      <h3 class="subhead">The people stay in charge</h3>
      <p>
        People stop being typists and line readers and become owners of intent, contracts and risk. Air traffic
        controllers are a good model: they don't fly the planes. They set routes, keep planes apart, and step in
        when something unusual happens.
      </p>
    </div>
    <dl class="jobs">
      {
        jobs.map((j) => (
          <div>
            <dt>{j.name}</dt>
            <dd>{j.body}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .agents-grid {
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 62rem) {
    .agents-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(0, 0.9fr);
      gap: 4rem;
    }
  }

  .asks ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .asks li {
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-paper);
    border-left: 8px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: var(--radius-strip);
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.9875rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .swap {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 1.5rem + 3vw, 4rem);
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 1rem + 1.6vw, 2.2rem);
    font-stretch: 108%;
    font-weight: 650;
    line-height: 1.18;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    max-width: 30ch;
  }

  .humans {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 2rem + 3vw, 4.5rem);
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 62rem) {
    .humans {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
      gap: 4rem;
    }
  }

  .jobs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 13rem), 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem 2rem;
  }

  .jobs dt {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .jobs dd {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.9875rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    margin-top: 0.2rem;
  }
</style>
